{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Opened an independent lead in the decision-support path: the leader verification counts acknowledgements from every replication peer, and the replication map is built for every server in the configuration including non-voters. A probe was written and locally verified that isolates the leader from the two other voters while keeping one non-voter wired; the setup event records that the voter is unreachable and the non-voter reachable with a voter quorum of two, and the result event records that VerifyLeader returned success. The experiment is queued for the fixed snapshot.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":960,\\\"end_line\\\":990,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":583,\\\"end_line\\\":650,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-heartbeat\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replication.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":385,\\\"end_line\\\":440,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@verifyleader-quorum\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\":\\\"Can the leader verification quorum be satisfied by acknowledgements from non-voters while a quorum of the voters in the configuration in force is unreachable?\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"s-heartbeat\\\"],\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"verifyLeader registers its future with every entry of the leader's replication map, and that map contains an entry for every server in the configuration, including non-voters; each peer's heartbeat acknowledges the verification, so a heartbeat from a non-voter can raise the vote count to the voter quorum even when no other voter is reachable.\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Demote one node of a four-peer cluster so the configuration is three voters plus one non-voter, isolate the leader from the other two voters while leaving the non-voter reachable, confirm that reachability with direct AppendEntries attempts, then call VerifyLeader and observe whether it returns success.\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@verifyleader-quorum\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"s-heartbeat\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A four-peer in-memory cluster with slowed timers is reduced to three voters plus one non-voter by demoting one follower; the leader is then disconnected from the two remaining voters in both directions while the non-voter stays wired, reachability is tested directly, and VerifyLeader is called with a bounded wait.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n    \\\"Cluster, transports and FSM are the repository's own MakeCluster, InmemTransport and MockFSM facilities; the demotion uses the public DemoteVoter API.\\\",\n    \\\"Timers are slowed for the probe so the leader lease does not step the leader down before the verification completes; the lease itself counts only voters.\\\",\n    \\\"Isolation is transport-level disconnection in both directions, and reachability is confirmed by direct AppendEntries attempts from the leader's transport.\\\"\n   ]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Start a four-peer cluster with one-second heartbeat and lease timers; wait for a leader and apply one command; DemoteVoter a follower so the configuration is three voters plus one non-voter; disconnect the leader from the other two voters in both directions; attempt one AppendEntries to the non-voter and one to a voter and record the errors; emit the setup event with the voters, the voter quorum, the two reachability results and the two node identifiers; call VerifyLeader in a goroutine with a five-second bound and emit the result event with whether it returned, its error, whether it succeeded, the elapsed time and the leader's state afterwards.\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"Leader verification must not report success unless a quorum of the voters of the configuration in force has acknowledged, so that a client cannot take the result as evidence that the node still leads the cluster.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"Raft itself: verifyLeader chooses which peers' acknowledgements count and the replication map it uses is built by the library.\\\",\n  \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"verifyLeader\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":966,\\\"end_line\\\":966},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startStopReplication\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":583,\\\"end_line\\\":583},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-heartbeat\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"heartbeat\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":388,\\\"end_line\\\":388}\n  ],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"verify-isolation-setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_leader_nonvoter_setup\\\",\n    \\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"voters_len\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n                  {\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_leader_nonvoter_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"verify-isolation-setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"verify_succeeded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Verification fails while only a non-voter can acknowledge.\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
