{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Opened and queued one more independent lead on the decision-support path: leader verification. Source reading shows verifyLeader registers its future with every entry of the leader's replication map, and that map is built for every server in the configuration including non-voters, while the leader lease (which correctly counts only voters) is what would otherwise bound the exposure. A probe was written and locally verified: with the configuration reduced to three voters plus one non-voter, the leader isolated from both other voters but still reaching the non-voter, direct AppendEntries confirmed the voter was unreachable and the non-voter reachable, and VerifyLeader returned success in under a millisecond with the leader still leading. The experiment is now requested against the fixed snapshot; that receipt is unread, so no account has been recorded for this question yet.\"}"}}
